window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-08641ec352c9249b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"migrate-a-validation-module\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">迁移一个验证模块</h1> <p>升级一个模块，并证明其公开行为仍然符合预期。</p> <p>为 Codex Cloud 提供范围明确的迁移说明、契约测试夹具和已准备好的云端环境。升级一个验证模块，并交付聚焦的代码更改、兼容性证据、剩余差异和回滚说明。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>迁移旧版验证组件的工程团队。</li> <li>已有明确契约和可重复测试的迁移工作。</li> <li>希望在其他模块继续工作的同时，审核一个小范围改动的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>迁移一个验证模块</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">在此云端环境中，将 [module]（位于 [repository]）从 [current pinned version] 迁移到 [approved target version]。\n\n首先阅读 AGENTS.md、[migration brief]、[official migration guide]、依赖锁定文件、此模块的调用方，以及 [contract test locations]。记录起始提交、环境/设置参考、已安装的 Python 版本、框架/Pydantic/内置 v1 版本，以及锁定文件的哈希。确认基线与目标版本兼容；将共享依赖或导入准备工作作为单独审核的更改处理。\n\n先运行 [baseline commands]，盘点迁移范围，并在 [plan file] 中编写简短计划。保留 [public contracts]。不要改动 [out-of-scope modules]。只在获准的代码范围内移除过时实现；明确列出必须保留的任何兼容适配器。\n\n如果可以隔离此代码范围且基线可用，就通过真实路由、错误处理器和响应序列化，在更改前后运行相同的冻结 HTTP 契约测试。比较状态码、契约要求的标头、接受/拒绝的输入、公开 JSON 键和类型、默认值/null 值，以及完整错误封装。也要运行受影响的集成测试、lint 和类型检查。如果这需要更广泛的升级或改变公开行为，应先报告这一决定，不要擅自扩大范围。不要批准新的快照、把公开差异规范化掉或削弱断言。记录每项检查对应的修订和环境/版本、前后命令、退出码、证据路径，以及附带限制的通过/失败/受阻/未运行状态。\n\n返回差异、前后证据、未解决的差异、依赖和锁定文件变更、回滚说明，以及一份草稿 PR 描述。仅当已连接的代码库工具和我的权限支持时，才创建草稿 PR；否则提供补丁和 PR 描述。不要合并、部署、修改生产数据，也不要开始另一个迁移范围。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">云端环境</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/migration/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pydantic 迁移指南（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面的 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"when-to-use-it\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">适用场景</h2> <p>当迁移范围清晰，并且已有测试可以比较新旧行为时，适合采用此工作流。向 Codex 提供迁移说明、模块及其调用方、冻结的契约测试夹具，以及已准备好的云端环境。要求它只做一项聚焦的改动，并提供证据和回滚途径。</p> <p>示例将订单服务中的一个验证模型从 <code>Pydantic</code> v1 迁移到 v2。示例包含原始实现、兼容性准备阶段和最终模块。测试会覆盖真实的 FastAPI 路由、错误处理器、响应序列化、相邻的旧版路由和公开 OpenAPI 文档。不包含数据库迁移或部署。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-cloud-environment\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">准备云端环境</h2> <ol> <li> <p>选择 <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong>，然后选择一个已发布的环境。</p> </li> <li> <p>若要新建环境，请选择 <strong>Create environment</strong>，选择 GitHub 代码库，并让 Codex 准备运行时、依赖项和隔离的测试服务。</p> </li> <li> <p>检查设置报告、解决失败的检查，并在开始新任务前选择 <strong>Publish</strong>。</p> </li> <li> <p>请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">当前云端环境指南</a>。</p> </li> <li>请将代码库指引保存在 <a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a> 中。</li> </ol> <p>如果依赖项或服务设置发生变化，请编辑可复用的环境、测试，然后选择 <strong>Republish</strong>。</p> <p>在一个新任务中验证更新后的环境。刷新代码库时会保留依赖缓存，不会重新运行安装或启动命令；现有任务仍保留各自的状态。</p> <p>请单独配置所需的网络目标和凭据。</p> <p>在每个阶段记录环境/设置参考、源代码提交、Python 补丁版本、框架和依赖版本、包管理器版本，以及锁定文件哈希。在新任务中使用这些结果之前，先核实相应版本。</p> <p><a id=\"run-the-sample\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">运行示例</h2> <p>下载<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/migrate-a-validation-module/sample.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">完整迁移示例（需联网）</a>。其中包含三个独立的 <code>uv</code> 项目、各自解析完成的 <code>uv.lock</code> 文件、应用实现、共享错误和模式适配器、冻结 HTTP 夹具以及契约运行器。</p> <p>使用 Python 3.11、3.12 或 3.13 并安装 <a href=\"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><code>uv</code>（需联网）</a>，然后运行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">unzip sample.zip\ncd migrate-a-validation-module\nuv run --project support/target --python python3 --frozen python run.py --compare-stages --output evidence\n</code></pre> <p>比较命令会为每个阶段创建独立的 <code>.venv</code>，并使用 <code>uv sync --frozen</code> 安装依赖。所有阶段都使用调用命令时选定的 Python 解释器和相同的 HTTP/模式夹具；依赖版本保持锁定。</p> <p>不包含 Python 3.14 及更高版本，因为旧版 <code>Pydantic</code> v1 桥接层不支持它们。成功运行时会以以下结果结束：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">PASS: legacy, prepared, target HTTP/schema/serialization contracts match\nNative model schemas differ; the existing public schema adapter is preserved.\n</code></pre> <p>请查看 <code>evidence/legacy.json</code>、<code>prepared.json</code>、<code>target.json</code> 和 <code>summary.json</code>。这些文件包含实际观察到的响应、运行时版本、源代码/夹具/锁定文件哈希、命令、退出码以及原始日志路径。</p> <p>运行器会通过 <code>FastAPI</code> 的进程内 <code>TestClient</code> 测试示例应用的 HTTP 端点。请在选定的 Cloud 任务中运行，并保留该任务的证据。</p> <p>只有在安装了 <code>Pydantic</code> v2 的环境中，才可不带 <code>--compare-stages</code> 运行 <code>python3 run.py</code>，以检查目标模型。这个独立模式检查七种验证和序列化情况，不运行 HTTP 或跨阶段兼容性检查。要验证迁移，请使用完整的比较命令。</p> <p>完整比较会检查每个阶段的 23 个 HTTP 用例、公开 OpenAPI 文档和响应序列化。它已在 Python 3.11、3.12 和 3.13 上通过本地测试。下载包中的 <code>README.md</code> 记录了已测试的版本和执行历史。请在 Cloud 环境中运行当前比较，并在那里记录结果。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-the-dependency-stages-separate\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">将不同依赖阶段分开</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>阶段</th> <th>Python / FastAPI / <code>Pydantic</code></th> <th>迁移范围</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>旧版</td> <td><code>3.11–3.13 / 0.119.0 / 1.10.22</code></td> <td>现有模型从 <code>pydantic</code> 导入。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>预备基线</td> <td><code>3.11–3.13 / 0.119.0 / 2.12.3</code></td> <td>两个模型都使用 <code>pydantic.v1</code>。记录实际内置的 v1 版本。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>目标版本</td> <td><code>3.11–3.13 / 0.119.0 / 2.12.3</code></td> <td>只有 <code>OrderInput</code> 迁移到 v2。相邻路由继续使用其独立的 v1 模型。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>预备阶段和目标阶段的依赖锁定完全相同。此模块范围内的改动只涉及模型及其直接序列化方法，不改变依赖环境。</p> <p>准备工作是单独审核的更改。它还会让剩余的 v1 路由适配器在响应验证之前，通过 <code>dict(by_alias=True)</code> 输出使用别名键的字典；在 v2 主环境中直接返回 v1 模型可能会丢失公开别名。</p> <p>目标订单适配器使用 <code>model_dump(by_alias=True)</code>，而相邻的 v1 路由继续使用其准备阶段适配器。</p> <p><a href=\"https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/how-to/migrate-from-pydantic-v1-to-pydantic-v2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">FastAPI 迁移指南（需联网）</a>将 v1/v2 混合路由的临时支持范围限定为 <code>0.119.0</code> 至 <code>0.127.x</code>；<code>0.128.0</code> 已移除这种支持。</p> <p>此示例特意固定在 <code>0.119.0</code>，用来演示这段过渡期。对于更新版本的 FastAPI 应用，请使用完整的 v2 边界，并为临时桥接层指定负责人和移除条件。不要嵌套 v1 和 v2 模型。此桥接层不能作为迁移到 Python 3.14 的方案。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-contract-tests\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">审查契约测试</h3> <p>冻结的 HTTP 用例覆盖成功请求、未提供 note 或明确将 note 设为 null、缺失和无效 ID、多个未知字段、混合字段错误、无效 note、格式错误的 JSON、错误的内容类型、缺少请求正文、别名、数组和字符串正文，以及相邻旧版路由。测试会比较状态码、<code>Content-Type</code> 标头和完整解析后的 JSON 响应，不会删除错误字段，也不会更改预期类型。</p> <p>此服务在旧版阶段就有自定义错误封装和公开 OpenAPI 文档。错误与模式适配器会继续保留。目标版本保持旧版错误顺序：先列出已声明字段的错误，再按字母顺序列出未知键。</p> <p>测试会比较完整且有序的 <code>error.fields</code> 数组，不会先对实际响应排序。运行器会分别记录每个模型自己的模式，并确认原生模式确实不同；公开模式保持一致，并不意味着依赖生成的模式完全相同。</p> <p>此服务保留一项旧版输入行为：它接受类似 <code>[[\"order_id\", \"ord_123\"]]</code> 的键值对数组作为对象；<code>[]</code> 和空 JSON 字符串都会变成空对象，并产生缺少 ID 的错误。非空字符串仍是无效请求正文。目标模型会保留成功执行 <code>dict(value)</code> 转换的行为。若要改为只接受对象，必须由负责人决定契约，而不能擅自改写测试预期。</p> <p>对于你自己的代码库，请在编辑之前冻结真实的现有响应。保留带显式默认值的可选字段，维持严格程度和未知字段行为，并测试真实的错误处理器与响应序列化。</p> <p>不同版本的原生验证错误会有所差异。<a href=\"https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/migration/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><code>Pydantic</code> 迁移指南（需联网）</a>还介绍了别名、强制转换、可选字段和自定义验证函数的变化；在这些函数内部抛出的 <code>TypeError</code> 在 v2 中不会被转换成 <code>ValidationError</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-the-contract-runner\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">检查契约运行器</h3> <p>下面的片段来自下载包中的 <code>run.py</code>。解压 ZIP 后，请运行完整文件；其中包含锁定的阶段和 HTTP 夹具。</p> <details> <summary>比较三个阶段</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">class OrderInput(BaseModel):\n    internal_order_id: StrictStr = Field(alias=\"order_id\")\n    customer_note: StrictStr | None = None\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", populate_by_name=False)\n\n    @model_validator(mode=\"before\")\n    @classmethod\n    def preserve_legacy_mapping(cls, value):\n        # v1 tries dict(value), so pairs, [] and \"\" can become objects.\n        # Preserve successful conversions without changing failed-input errors.\n        if not isinstance(value, dict):\n            try:\n                return dict(value)\n            except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                return value\n        return value\n\n\ndef serialize_order(payload):\n    return OrderInput(**payload).model_dump(by_alias=True)\n\n\ndef preserve_legacy_error_order(fields):\n    # v1 reports declared-field errors first and unknown keys alphabetically.\n    # v2 keeps unknown keys in input order; preserve the existing HTTP contract.\n    known = [field for field in fields if field[\"code\"] != \"extra_forbidden\"]\n    extra = sorted(\n        (field for field in fields if field[\"code\"] == \"extra_forbidden\"),\n        key=lambda field: field[\"path\"],\n    )\n    return known + extra\n\n\ndef check_target_model():\n    for payload, expected in (\n        ({\"order_id\": \"ord_123\"}, {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": None}),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": \"Leave at desk\"},\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": \"Leave at desk\"},\n        ),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": None},\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": None},\n        ),\n    ):\n        assert serialize_order(payload) == expected\n    for payload, expected in (\n        ({}, [(\"order_id\", \"missing\")]),\n        ({\"order_id\": 123}, [(\"order_id\", \"string_type\")]),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": 17},\n            [(\"customer_note\", \"string_type\")],\n        ),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"unexpected\": True},\n            [(\"unexpected\", \"extra_forbidden\")],\n        ),\n    ):\n        try:\n            OrderInput(**payload)\n        except ValidationError as error:\n            assert [\n                (item[\"loc\"][0], item[\"type\"]) for item in error.errors()\n            ] == expected\n        else:\n            raise AssertionError(f\"Accepted invalid order: {payload}\")\n    print(\"PASS: target model validation and serialization (7 cases)\")\n    print(\"Model-only checks; use --compare-stages for HTTP migration parity.\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path, default=ROOT / \"evidence\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--compare-stages\", action=\"store_true\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    if not args.compare_stages:\n        check_target_model()\n        return\n    args.output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    reports = []\n    commands = []\n    for stage in (\"legacy\", \"prepared\", \"target\"):\n        project = Path(\"support\") / stage\n        stage_commands = [\n            [\n                \"uv\",\n                \"sync\",\n                \"--project\",\n                str(project),\n                \"--python\",\n                sys.executable,\n                \"--frozen\",\n            ],\n            [\n                \"uv\",\n                \"run\",\n                \"--project\",\n                str(project),\n                \"--python\",\n                sys.executable,\n                \"--frozen\",\n                \"python\",\n                \"test/run_stage.py\",\n                stage,\n                str(args.output / f\"{stage}.json\"),\n            ],\n        ]\n        for command in stage_commands:\n            completed = subprocess.run(\n                command, cwd=ROOT, capture_output=True, text=True\n            )\n            label = f\"{stage}-{len(commands)}\"\n            (args.output / f\"{label}.log\").write_text(\n                completed.stdout + completed.stderr\n            )\n            commands.append(\n                {\n                    \"command\": command,\n                    \"exit_code\": completed.returncode,\n                    \"log\": f\"{label}.log\",\n                }\n            )\n            (args.output / \"commands.json\").write_text(\n                json.dumps(commands, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\"\n            )\n            if completed.returncode:\n                print(completed.stdout + completed.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\n                raise SystemExit(completed.returncode)\n            print(completed.stdout, end=\"\")\n        reports.append(json.loads((args.output / f\"{stage}.json\").read_text()))\n    assert all(report[\"python\"] == platform.python_version() for report in reports)\n    for report in reports[1:]:\n        for key in (\n            \"observations\",\n            \"public_openapi\",\n            \"direct_call\",\n            \"fixture_sha256\",\n            \"schema_fixture_sha256\",\n        ):\n            assert report[key] == reports[0][key], f\"Parity failed: {key}\"\n    assert reports[1][\"lock_sha256\"] == reports[2][\"lock_sha256\"]\n    native_schema_differs = (\n        reports[0][\"native_model_schema\"] != reports[2][\"native_model_schema\"]\n    )\n    assert native_schema_differs, \"The example should expose native schema drift\"\n    manifest = {\n        str(path.relative_to(ROOT)): digest(path)\n        for path in sorted(ROOT.rglob(\"*\"))\n        if path.is_file()\n        and not path.resolve().is_relative_to(args.output.resolve())\n        and not any(\n            part in {\".venv\", \"__pycache__\", \"evidence\", \".ruff_cache\"}\n            for part in path.relative_to(ROOT).parts\n        )\n    }\n    summary = {\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"scope\": \"synthetic in-process FastAPI TestClient execution\",\n        \"stages\": [report[\"stage\"] for report in reports],\n        \"http_cases_per_stage\": reports[0][\"http_cases\"],\n        \"native_model_schema_differs\": native_schema_differs,\n        \"public_http_and_schema_parity\": True,\n        \"commands\": commands,\n        \"source_sha256\": manifest,\n    }\n    (args.output / \"summary.json\").write_text(\n        json.dumps(summary, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\"\n    )\n    print(\"PASS: legacy, prepared, target HTTP/schema/serialization contracts match\")\n    print(\n        \"Native model schemas differ; the existing public schema adapter is preserved.\"\n    )\n</code></pre> </details> <p><a id=\"run-the-workflow-in-your-repository\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">在你自己的代码库中运行工作流</h2> <ol> <li><strong>编写迁移说明。</strong> 写明模块、直接调用方、负责人、批准的版本、契约测试、不在范围内的代码和回滚说明。如果迁移需要扩大依赖升级范围或改变公开行为，请停下来。</li> <li><strong>建立基线。</strong> 让 Codex 阅读 <code>AGENTS.md</code>、迁移说明、官方迁移指引、锁定文件、调用方和测试。记录起始提交和已安装的版本。在声称兼容之前，说明或修复失败的基线检查。</li> <li><strong>单独准备兼容性。</strong> 如果共享依赖会影响其他代码，先单独审核准备工作。证明相同的夹具在原始基线和预备基线上都能通过。</li> <li><strong>迁移一个范围。</strong> 使用本页的起始提示词。修改该模块及其直接适配器；保留不相关的模块，并说明仍保留的任何兼容代码。</li> <li><strong>运行相同的测试。</strong> 不改变预期，对比基线和最终版的 HTTP/模式夹具。运行受影响的集成、lint 和类型检查，并保存与最终源代码及依赖状态绑定的输出。</li> <li><strong>审核交接材料。</strong> 检查差异、实际观察到的证据、未解决差异、剩余的桥接代码和回滚方法。只有代码库工具和权限支持时才创建草稿 PR。将合并、部署和下一项迁移留给审核者。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"record-what-was-verified\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">记录已验证的内容</h2> <p>每项标准都应有一条证据记录：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Criterion: [behavior and test]\nEnvironment: [setup reference; actual runtime and dependency versions]\nBefore: [commit/diff ID; command; exit code; observed result; evidence path]\nAfter: [final commit/diff ID; command; exit code; observed result; evidence path]\nStatus: [pass / fail / blocked / not run]\nLimits: [untested behavior, missing prerequisite, or required owner decision]\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>模板中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">验收标准：[behavior and test]\n环境：[setup reference; actual runtime and dependency versions]\n修改前：[commit/diff ID; command; exit code; observed result; evidence path]\n修改后：[final commit/diff ID; command; exit code; observed result; evidence path]\n状态：[pass / fail / blocked / not run]\n局限：[untested behavior, missing prerequisite, or required owner decision]</div></div> <p>导入成功、lint 检查通过或重新生成快照，都不能单独证明 API 兼容。应单独记录有意保留的差异；如果最终源代码发生变化，就重新运行检查。改编示例时，契约测试还应覆盖你的应用调用方和服务。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"migrate-a-validation-module\">Migrate a validation module</h1> <p>Upgrade one module and prove that its public behavior still holds.</p> <p>Give Codex a bounded migration brief, contract fixtures, and a prepared cloud environment. Upgrade one validation module and return the focused change, parity evidence, remaining differences, and rollback instructions.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Engineering teams moving a legacy validation component.</li> <li>Migrations with explicit contracts and repeatable tests.</li> <li>Teams needing a small reviewed change while other modules keep working.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Migrate a validation module</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Migrate [module] in [repository] from [current pinned version] to [approved target version] in this cloud environment.\n\nRead AGENTS.md, [migration brief], [official migration guide], the dependency lockfile, the module's callers, and [contract test locations]. Record the starting commit, environment/setup reference, installed Python version, framework/Pydantic/bundled-v1 versions, and lockfile hash. Confirm baseline/target compatibility; treat shared dependency/import preparation as a separate reviewed change.\n\nFirst run [baseline commands], inventory the migration surface, and write a short plan in [plan file]. Preserve [public contracts]. Keep [out-of-scope modules] unchanged. Remove obsolete code only inside the approved slice; name any compatibility adapter that must remain.\n\nIf the slice can be isolated and the baseline is usable, run the same frozen HTTP contract tests before and after the change through the real router, error handler, and response serialization. Compare status codes, contractual headers, accepted/rejected inputs, public JSON keys/types, defaults/nulls, and the complete error envelope. Run affected integration, lint and type checks too. If this requires broader upgrades or public behavior changes, return that decision before expanding scope. Do not approve new snapshots, normalize away public differences or weaken assertions. Record each check's revisions/environment/versions, before/after commands, exit codes, evidence paths, and pass/fail/blocked/not run with limitations.\n\nReturn the diff, before-and-after evidence, unresolved differences, dependency and lockfile changes, rollback instructions, and a draft PR description. Create a draft PR only if the connected repository tools and my permissions support it; otherwise provide the patch and description. Do not merge, deploy, change production data, or begin another slice.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Cloud environments</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/migration/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pydantic migration guide (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"when-to-use-it\">When to use it</h2> <p>Use this workflow when a migration has a clear boundary and tests that compare old and new behavior. Give Codex a migration brief, the module and its callers, frozen contract fixtures, and a prepared cloud environment. Ask for one focused change with evidence and a rollback path.</p> <p>The sample migrates one validation model in an orders service from <code>Pydantic</code> v1 to v2. It includes the original implementation, a compatibility preparation stage, and the final module. Its tests exercise the real FastAPI router, error handler, response serialization, adjacent legacy route, and public OpenAPI document. No database migration or deployment is included.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-cloud-environment\">Prepare the cloud environment</h2> <ol> <li> <p>Choose <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong> and select a published environment.</p> </li> <li> <p>To create one, select <strong>Create environment</strong>, choose the GitHub repositories, and ask Codex to prepare the runtime, dependencies, and isolated test services.</p> </li> <li> <p>Review the setup report, resolve failed checks, and <strong>Publish</strong> before starting a new task.</p> </li> <li> <p>Follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Cloud environment guide</a>.</p> </li> <li>Keep repository guidance in <a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a>.</li> </ol> <p>If dependencies change or service setup changes, edit the reusable environment, test it, and <strong>Republish</strong>.</p> <p>Validate the updated environment in a new task. Repository refresh preserves dependency caches without rerunning installation or startup commands, and existing tasks retain their own state.</p> <p>Configure required network destinations and credentials separately.</p> <p>Record the environment/setup reference, source commit, Python patch version, framework and dependency versions, package-manager version, and lockfile hash at each stage. Verify those versions inside the new task before using its results.</p> <h2 id=\"run-the-sample\">Run the sample</h2> <p>Download the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/migrate-a-validation-module/sample.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">complete migration sample (online)</a>. It includes three standalone <code>uv</code> projects, their resolved <code>uv.lock</code> files, application implementations, a shared error and schema adapter, frozen HTTP fixtures, and the contract runner.</p> <p>Use Python 3.11, 3.12, or 3.13 and install <a href=\"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><code>uv</code> (online)</a>, then run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">unzip sample.zip\ncd migrate-a-validation-module\nuv run --project support/target --python python3 --frozen python run.py --compare-stages --output evidence\n</code></pre> <p>The comparison creates a separate <code>.venv</code> for each stage and installs dependencies with <code>uv sync --frozen</code>. All stages use the invoking Python interpreter and the same HTTP and schema fixtures; dependency versions remain locked.</p> <p>Python 3.14 and later are excluded because the legacy <code>Pydantic</code> v1 bridge does not support them. A successful run ends with:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">PASS: legacy, prepared, target HTTP/schema/serialization contracts match\nNative model schemas differ; the existing public schema adapter is preserved.\n</code></pre> <p>Read <code>evidence/legacy.json</code>, <code>prepared.json</code>, <code>target.json</code>, and <code>summary.json</code>. They contain observed responses, runtime versions, source, fixture, and lockfile hashes, commands, exit codes, and raw-log paths.</p> <p>The runner exercises the sample application's HTTP endpoints through <code>FastAPI</code>'s in-process <code>TestClient</code>. Run it inside your chosen Cloud task and retain that task's evidence.</p> <p>Run <code>python3 run.py</code> without <code>--compare-stages</code> only to check the target model in an environment with <code>Pydantic</code> v2 installed. That self-contained mode checks seven validation and serialization cases. It does not run HTTP or cross-stage parity checks. Use the full comparison command above to verify a migration.</p> <p>The full comparison checks 23 HTTP cases in each stage, public OpenAPI, and response serialization. It passed locally on Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13. The download's <code>README.md</code> records the tested versions and execution history. Run the current comparison in your Cloud environment to record its results there.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-the-dependency-stages-separate\">Keep the dependency stages separate</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Stage</th> <th>Python / FastAPI / <code>Pydantic</code></th> <th>Migration boundary</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Legacy</td> <td><code>3.11–3.13 / 0.119.0 / 1.10.22</code></td> <td>Existing models import from <code>pydantic</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Prepared baseline</td> <td><code>3.11–3.13 / 0.119.0 / 2.12.3</code></td> <td>Both models use <code>pydantic.v1</code>. Record the actual bundled-v1 version.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Target</td> <td><code>3.11–3.13 / 0.119.0 / 2.12.3</code></td> <td>Only <code>OrderInput</code> moves to v2. The adjacent route keeps its separate v1 model.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The prepared and target dependency locks are identical. The module slice changes the model and its direct serialization method, not the dependency environment.</p> <p>The preparation step is a separate reviewed change. It also makes the remaining v1 route adapters emit alias-keyed dictionaries with <code>dict(by_alias=True)</code> before response validation; returning the v1 model directly under the v2 host can lose public aliases.</p> <p>The target order adapter uses <code>model_dump(by_alias=True)</code>, and the adjacent v1 route keeps its preparation adapter.</p> <p>The <a href=\"https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/how-to/migrate-from-pydantic-v1-to-pydantic-v2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">FastAPI migration guide (online)</a> limits temporary mixed v1/v2 route support to <code>0.119.0</code> through <code>0.127.x</code>; <code>0.128.0</code> removed it.</p> <p>This example deliberately pins <code>0.119.0</code> to demonstrate that transition. Use a fully v2 boundary for a newer FastAPI application, and keep an owner and removal condition for the temporary bridge. Do not nest v1 and v2 models. This bridge is not a Python 3.14 migration path.</p> <h3 id=\"review-the-contract-tests\">Review the contract tests</h3> <p>The frozen HTTP cases cover successful requests, an omitted note or a note explicitly set to null, missing and invalid IDs, multiple unknown fields, mixed field errors, invalid notes, malformed JSON, wrong content type, missing body, aliases, array and string bodies, and the adjacent legacy route. They compare status codes, the <code>Content-Type</code> header, and complete parsed JSON responses without stripping error fields or changing expected types.</p> <p>The service has an application-owned error envelope and public OpenAPI document from the legacy stage. The error and schema adapters remain in place. The target preserves the legacy error order: declared-field errors first, then unknown keys alphabetically.</p> <p>The tests compare the complete ordered <code>error.fields</code> array; they do not sort observed responses. The runner records each model's native schema separately and verifies that native schemas differ; public schema parity does not mean the dependency's generated schemas are identical.</p> <p>The service preserves a legacy input behavior: it accepts an array of pairs such as <code>[[\"order_id\", \"ord_123\"]]</code> as an object, and both <code>[]</code> and an empty JSON string become empty objects with a missing-ID error. A nonempty string remains an invalid body. The target model keeps successful <code>dict(value)</code> conversions. Changing it to object-only input requires an owner's contract decision, not a rewritten test expectation.</p> <p>For your repository, freeze its actual existing responses before editing. Preserve optional fields with explicit defaults, keep strictness and unknown-field behavior, and test the real error handler and response serialization.</p> <p>Raw validation errors differ across versions. The <a href=\"https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/migration/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><code>Pydantic</code> migration guide (online)</a> also describes changes to aliases, coercion, optional fields, and custom validation functions; v2 does not convert <code>TypeError</code> raised inside those functions into <code>ValidationError</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-the-contract-runner\">Inspect the contract runner</h3> <p>This excerpt comes from <code>run.py</code> in the download. Run the complete files after extracting the ZIP; the locked stages and HTTP fixtures are included there.</p> <details> <summary>Compare the three stages</summary> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">class OrderInput(BaseModel):\n    internal_order_id: StrictStr = Field(alias=\"order_id\")\n    customer_note: StrictStr | None = None\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", populate_by_name=False)\n\n    @model_validator(mode=\"before\")\n    @classmethod\n    def preserve_legacy_mapping(cls, value):\n        # v1 tries dict(value), so pairs, [] and \"\" can become objects.\n        # Preserve successful conversions without changing failed-input errors.\n        if not isinstance(value, dict):\n            try:\n                return dict(value)\n            except (TypeError, ValueError):\n                return value\n        return value\n\n\ndef serialize_order(payload):\n    return OrderInput(**payload).model_dump(by_alias=True)\n\n\ndef preserve_legacy_error_order(fields):\n    # v1 reports declared-field errors first and unknown keys alphabetically.\n    # v2 keeps unknown keys in input order; preserve the existing HTTP contract.\n    known = [field for field in fields if field[\"code\"] != \"extra_forbidden\"]\n    extra = sorted(\n        (field for field in fields if field[\"code\"] == \"extra_forbidden\"),\n        key=lambda field: field[\"path\"],\n    )\n    return known + extra\n\n\ndef check_target_model():\n    for payload, expected in (\n        ({\"order_id\": \"ord_123\"}, {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": None}),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": \"Leave at desk\"},\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": \"Leave at desk\"},\n        ),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": None},\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": None},\n        ),\n    ):\n        assert serialize_order(payload) == expected\n    for payload, expected in (\n        ({}, [(\"order_id\", \"missing\")]),\n        ({\"order_id\": 123}, [(\"order_id\", \"string_type\")]),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"customer_note\": 17},\n            [(\"customer_note\", \"string_type\")],\n        ),\n        (\n            {\"order_id\": \"ord_123\", \"unexpected\": True},\n            [(\"unexpected\", \"extra_forbidden\")],\n        ),\n    ):\n        try:\n            OrderInput(**payload)\n        except ValidationError as error:\n            assert [\n                (item[\"loc\"][0], item[\"type\"]) for item in error.errors()\n            ] == expected\n        else:\n            raise AssertionError(f\"Accepted invalid order: {payload}\")\n    print(\"PASS: target model validation and serialization (7 cases)\")\n    print(\"Model-only checks; use --compare-stages for HTTP migration parity.\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path, default=ROOT / \"evidence\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--compare-stages\", action=\"store_true\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    if not args.compare_stages:\n        check_target_model()\n        return\n    args.output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    reports = []\n    commands = []\n    for stage in (\"legacy\", \"prepared\", \"target\"):\n        project = Path(\"support\") / stage\n        stage_commands = [\n            [\n                \"uv\",\n                \"sync\",\n                \"--project\",\n                str(project),\n                \"--python\",\n                sys.executable,\n                \"--frozen\",\n            ],\n            [\n                \"uv\",\n                \"run\",\n                \"--project\",\n                str(project),\n                \"--python\",\n                sys.executable,\n                \"--frozen\",\n                \"python\",\n                \"test/run_stage.py\",\n                stage,\n                str(args.output / f\"{stage}.json\"),\n            ],\n        ]\n        for command in stage_commands:\n            completed = subprocess.run(\n                command, cwd=ROOT, capture_output=True, text=True\n            )\n            label = f\"{stage}-{len(commands)}\"\n            (args.output / f\"{label}.log\").write_text(\n                completed.stdout + completed.stderr\n            )\n            commands.append(\n                {\n                    \"command\": command,\n                    \"exit_code\": completed.returncode,\n                    \"log\": f\"{label}.log\",\n                }\n            )\n            (args.output / \"commands.json\").write_text(\n                json.dumps(commands, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\"\n            )\n            if completed.returncode:\n                print(completed.stdout + completed.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\n                raise SystemExit(completed.returncode)\n            print(completed.stdout, end=\"\")\n        reports.append(json.loads((args.output / f\"{stage}.json\").read_text()))\n    assert all(report[\"python\"] == platform.python_version() for report in reports)\n    for report in reports[1:]:\n        for key in (\n            \"observations\",\n            \"public_openapi\",\n            \"direct_call\",\n            \"fixture_sha256\",\n            \"schema_fixture_sha256\",\n        ):\n            assert report[key] == reports[0][key], f\"Parity failed: {key}\"\n    assert reports[1][\"lock_sha256\"] == reports[2][\"lock_sha256\"]\n    native_schema_differs = (\n        reports[0][\"native_model_schema\"] != reports[2][\"native_model_schema\"]\n    )\n    assert native_schema_differs, \"The example should expose native schema drift\"\n    manifest = {\n        str(path.relative_to(ROOT)): digest(path)\n        for path in sorted(ROOT.rglob(\"*\"))\n        if path.is_file()\n        and not path.resolve().is_relative_to(args.output.resolve())\n        and not any(\n            part in {\".venv\", \"__pycache__\", \"evidence\", \".ruff_cache\"}\n            for part in path.relative_to(ROOT).parts\n        )\n    }\n    summary = {\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"scope\": \"synthetic in-process FastAPI TestClient execution\",\n        \"stages\": [report[\"stage\"] for report in reports],\n        \"http_cases_per_stage\": reports[0][\"http_cases\"],\n        \"native_model_schema_differs\": native_schema_differs,\n        \"public_http_and_schema_parity\": True,\n        \"commands\": commands,\n        \"source_sha256\": manifest,\n    }\n    (args.output / \"summary.json\").write_text(\n        json.dumps(summary, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\"\n    )\n    print(\"PASS: legacy, prepared, target HTTP/schema/serialization contracts match\")\n    print(\n        \"Native model schemas differ; the existing public schema adapter is preserved.\"\n    )\n</code></pre> </details> <h2 id=\"run-the-workflow-in-your-repository\">Run the workflow in your repository</h2> <ol> <li><strong>Write the brief.</strong> Name the module, direct callers, owner, approved versions, contract tests, out-of-scope code, and rollback instructions. Stop if the slice requires a wider dependency upgrade or changes public behavior.</li> <li><strong>Establish the baseline.</strong> Have Codex read <code>AGENTS.md</code>, the brief, official migration guidance, locks, callers, and tests. Record the starting commit and installed versions. Explain or repair failing baseline checks before claiming parity.</li> <li><strong>Prepare compatibility separately.</strong> If shared dependencies couple the module to other code, review that preparation first. Prove that the same fixtures pass against both the original and prepared baselines.</li> <li><strong>Migrate one slice.</strong> Use the starter prompt on this page. Change the module and its direct adapter; preserve unrelated modules and name any compatibility code that remains.</li> <li><strong>Run the same tests.</strong> Compare baseline and final HTTP/schema fixtures without changing expectations. Run affected integration, lint, and type checks, and save output tied to the final source and dependency state.</li> <li><strong>Review the handoff.</strong> Inspect the diff, observed evidence, unresolved differences, remaining bridge, and rollback. Create a draft PR only when repository tools and permissions support it. Leave merging, deployment, and another migration slice to the reviewer.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"record-what-was-verified\">Record what was verified</h2> <p>Use an evidence record for each criterion:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Criterion: [behavior and test]\nEnvironment: [setup reference; actual runtime and dependency versions]\nBefore: [commit/diff ID; command; exit code; observed result; evidence path]\nAfter: [final commit/diff ID; command; exit code; observed result; evidence path]\nStatus: [pass / fail / blocked / not run]\nLimits: [untested behavior, missing prerequisite, or required owner decision]\n</code></pre> <p>A successful import, lint check, or regenerated snapshot does not prove API parity. Record intentional differences separately, and rerun checks when the final source changes. When adapting the sample, include your application's callers and services in the contract tests.</p>"};
